@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] browser-helper-current-url-only
The helper MUST show only for a currently foregrounded supported browser whose native
address field supplies a complete GitHub repository URL. It MUST NOT infer the current
URL from page links, titles, arbitrary text, clipboard or history. Missing, focused,
hidden, malformed, conflicting or web-content address fields MUST hide the button.
Window and navigation changes MUST discard the old observation, and a tap MUST verify
the current browser window and repository again before opening Pully (Tavi, 18 Oct 2026,
"it does it by checking the URL somehow").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] browser-helper-opt-in-and-local
The service MUST require both the in-app disclosure consent and the reader's Android
accessibility grant, plus the device-local experimental opt-in. Existing grants or old
consent MUST NOT opt into the experiment. With either opt-in off, interruption, service disconnect, screen lock,
or another app in front, the overlay MUST be removed. The helper MUST NOT persist or log
browsing URLs, inspect page content, request screenshot or gesture capabilities, or make
network requests. Only the normalized repository MAY be handed to Pully on an explicit
tap; Pully's normal repository connection then applies (Tavi, 18 Oct 2026). Only a
successful explicit tap MAY record the fixed experiment/action enums through the
existing analytics opt-out boundary; observations MUST NOT emit analytics. The
experimental gate and tap-only usage counting are Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 follow-up.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:design;architecture] browser-helper-native-overlay
The cross-app helper MAY use a native TextView in TYPE_ACCESSIBILITY_OVERLAY because
it has no Activity or Compose lifecycle. Its colours, type size, space and radius MUST
come from Pully's existing design tokens and chosen theme. It MUST NOT request the
separate draw-over-other-apps permission (Tavi, 18 Oct 2026, accessibility helper request;
DESIGN.md rules 1, 11 and 47).
